;
; log's dk = (double)k without L2D: an add to the bits and an exact subtraction
; (PROOFS.md, L8).
;
; e_log.c (reference/fdlibm-5.3) converts its int k to double, dk = (double)k (lines
; 115, 118 and 122). The port (Log) holds k in a long lane, and C2 lowers no L2D on AVX2,
; so it computes dk = fromBits(k + DK_MAGIC_BITS) - DK_MAGIC, with DK_MAGIC = 0x1.8p52
; and DK_MAGIC_BITS = 0x43380000_00000000 its bits, both rendered from Log. The claim: for
; every long k in [-2^51, 2^51), that is the double whose value is k, which for k = 0 is
; +0.
;
; What is proven: DK_MAGIC's bits are DK_MAGIC (S = 1, binade 2^52,
; M = 6755399441055744, ulp 1); for every k in the domain, k + DK_MAGIC_BITS (jlong.add, so a wrap would show) has S = 1,
; E = 0 and M = 6755399441055744 + k, the double 0x1.8p52 + k; so the exact difference less DK_MAGIC
; is the integer k; and for k in each binade 2^0 to 2^51, either sign, k rounds to the
; double S * |k| * 2^(52 - j) * 2^(j - 52) whose value is k, and to no other double in
; that binade or the next ones. The domain is tight: at k = 2^51 the bits carry into
; the exponent and k = 2^51 + 1 gives 2^51 + 2; and DK_MAGIC_BITS + 1 gives k + 1.
;
; What is not: that the double named is Java's (double)k, which JLS 5.1.2 makes exact for
; |k| <= 2^53 (ProofsTest.l8ExactConversionIsI2D compares the bits); that for k = 0 the
; exact zero difference x - x is +0 (IEEE 754 6.3, pinned in log_zero_dk.smt2's section
; A only for like-signed zeros, here stated); that a value rounds to no double in a binade
; further off than the next one (the arithmetic of rationals); that log's k lies in the
; domain, which log_long_words.smt2 proves for every lane; and that the port computes
; this, the code's text.
;
; The logic is ALL: the per-binade checks are those of exp_zero_reduction.smt2.
;
; Rendered by ProofFiles (src/test/java). ProofFilesTest fails when this file differs from
; its rendering, and mvn -q test -Dtest=ProofFilesTest -Dvfdlibm.proofs.regen=true
; rewrites it. Run by dev/prove.sh, which inserts java.smt2 after the set-logic line.

(set-logic ALL)

(echo "DK_MAGIC_BITS = 0x43380000_00000000 is 0x1.8p52: S = 1, E = 0, M = 3 * 2^51: expect unsat")
(push 1)
(assert (not (and (= (jdouble.fromBits.S 4843621399236968448) 1)
  (= (jdouble.fromBits.E 4843621399236968448) 0)
  (= (jdouble.fromBits.M 4843621399236968448) 6755399441055744)
  (= 6755399441055744 (* 3 2251799813685248)))))
(check-sat)
(pop 1)

(echo "for k in [-2^51, 2^51), k + DK_MAGIC_BITS is the double 0x1.8p52 + k: expect unsat")
(push 1)
(declare-const k Int)
(assert (and (<= (- 2251799813685248) k) (< k 2251799813685248)))
(assert (not (and (= (jdouble.fromBits.S (jlong.add k 4843621399236968448)) 1) (=
  (jdouble.fromBits.E (jlong.add k 4843621399236968448)) 0)
  (= (jdouble.fromBits.M (jlong.add k 4843621399236968448)) (+ 6755399441055744 k)))))
(check-sat)
(pop 1)

